{"evidence":["Reviewed crates/tank_core/src/save.rs: save loading now uses an ordered migration registry with a compile-time length invariant, applies migrations sequentially from the file version to SCHEMA_VERSION, and stamps migrated saves to the current schema before deserialization.","Reviewed crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs: unknown future saves and unsupported old saves now return explicit, human-readable SimError variants instead of falling through to a generic mismatch path.","Reviewed crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs: coverage includes v2->current migration, legacy saves missing stability_tracker, future-version rejection, too-old rejection, zero-version rejection, and save/load determinism after restore.","Verified the implementation in the workspace with `cargo test`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`, and `cargo fmt --check`; all passed.","The migration contract is documented inline next to the registry in crates/tank_core/src/save.rs, including how later phases should append migrations and keep the version chain contiguous."],"findings_or_gaps":[],"follow_up_or_amendments":[],"outcome":"approved"}